{"reasoning":"Florence and Edgar guessed identically in 9 of 10 rounds, which looks suspicious at first. Most of that matching is explained by the shared public intersection method, since all four players converged in rounds 4, 5, 9 and 10.

The early rounds are the strongest signal. In round 1 the only shared ranges were Edgar's 13-52 and Helen's 45-84, whose intersection is 45-52 (midpoint 48.5). Florence and Edgar both guessed 48 and William 49, so all three followed the open information and the match is not exclusive. In round 2 the public intersection was 40-41 (from 12-51, 3-42, 2-41 and 40-79). Florence and Edgar both picked 41 while Helen and William picked 40, a coin-flip coincidence.

In round 7 the public intersection was 47-48. Florence and Edgar guessed 48 and William 47, while Helen stayed at 56. Florence also had the highest total, 18. The repeated identical guesses give mild evidence for Florence+Edgar, but it is ambiguous because the open sharing explains most of it.","probabilities":{"Florence+Edgar":0.35,"Florence+Helen":0.05,"Florence+William":0.05,"Edgar+Helen":0.04,"Edgar+William":0.05,"Helen+William":0.04,"none":0.42}}

{"reasoning":"William's messages contain odd numeric codes (temperatures, 'chair' numbers) that look like an encoding, but the record should show who acts on them. Several of his numbers behave like range endpoints. R1 '48' would give a range of 9 to 48 with midpoint about 28.5, close to his own guess of 25. R3 '48' and '87' read as a 48-87 range with midpoint 67.5. R4 '64' and '103' read as 64-103, midpoint 83.5, and the secret was 81. R5 '-5' and '34' give midpoint 14.5, with secret 33. R7 '-10' and '29' give midpoint 9.5, secret 21. The pattern is roughly consistent: two numbers 39 apart, i.e. a 40-wide range.

Who uses it? R4: Mina's own range was 40-79 and she guessed 72 rather than her stated 65, which fits combining with William's 64-103 (overlap 64-79, midpoint about 71.5). Eusapia guessed 88 versus her stated 97, which also fits combining with William's range. R5: William's range -5 to 34 overlaps Mina's 20-60 in 20-34, and Mina guessed 36, below her stated 40. Eusapia guessed 40 as stated. R7: William's code says up to 29 and Eusapia guessed exactly 29, but she had also stated 29 in her message. Mina guessed 38 versus her stated 45, overlapping 25-29. Helen guessed 28 despite saying 9, perhaps from Mina's 25-64 combined with her own information. R3: Mina guessed 88 versus her stated 98, about 10 lower. William's range 48-87 overlaps 'high nineties' only near 87, so a guess of 88 fits that combination well.

Mina's guesses consistently shift toward William's coded ranges, and William's guesses also fit Mina's ranges: R2 22 fits neither, but R4 89, R5 30 and R6 34 do. Mina also openly states her ranges. William+Mina looks most likely.","probabilities":{"William+Mina":0.45,"William+Eusapia":0.2,"William+Helen":0.1,"Mina+Eusapia":0.05,"Mina+Helen":0.05,"Eusapia+Helen":0.03,"none":0.12}}

{"reasoning":"Edgar and Eusapia use a matching coded framing. Each posts a short line of the form 'The X starts/begins at N' that looks like the lower end of a range, which they don't explain to the table, while Charles states his ranges openly. Their messages are near-copies of each other. Eusapia's R4 text later reappears in R7, R8 and R9, and in R6 she repeats Edgar's R5 message almost word for word. Edgar also starts using phrasing from Eusapia's R5 message.

Their guesses fit the code. In R1, Edgar posted 'starts at 16' (range 16-55); combined with Charles's open -9 to 30, that gives an overlap of 16-30. Eusapia guessed 22, near the middle of that overlap. In R7, Edgar posted 17 (range 17-56); with Charles's -8 to 31, the overlap is 17-31, and Eusapia guessed 24. Edgar's guesses also fit the overlap of Eusapia's and Charles's numbers. For example, in R8, Eusapia's 38 (range 38-77) overlaps Charles's 12-51 at 38-51, and Edgar guessed 45.

The evidence points strongly to Edgar+Eusapia.","probabilities":{"Edgar+Arthur":0.02,"Edgar+Charles":0.02,"Edgar+Eusapia":0.9,"Arthur+Charles":0.01,"Arthur+Eusapia":0.02,"Charles+Eusapia":0.01,"none":0.02}}

{"reasoning":"Most players openly share their ranges and then guess near the intersection of everyone's ranges. Arthur, Emma and Edgar often converge on the same guess, which is consistent with all three combining the public information. William is the odd one out: he often guesses his own midpoint. That pattern does not single out any pair.

Two details are worth checking. In round 1 William gave no range but said 'around 64'. If his range were 44-83, the intersection with Arthur (29-68), Emma (9-48) and Edgar (around 21-60) would be 44-48, and nobody exploited that. In round 9 Arthur and Edgar both guessed 88 while Emma guessed 91. The intersection of 82-100 with Emma's 60-99 and William's 54-93 is 82-93, whose midpoint is about 87-88, so Arthur and Edgar computed it correctly. Emma guessing 91 was simply suboptimal. Their round 9 messages were nearly identical, but both sets of public information support that match.

Finally, Arthur and Edgar have the top totals (19.5 and 17), but their scores are explained by sound use of the shared information. There is no strong pair-specific evidence, so 'none' is favored.","probabilities":{"Arthur+Emma":0.07,"Arthur+William":0.05,"Arthur+Edgar":0.13,"Emma+William":0.04,"Emma+Edgar":0.07,"William+Edgar":0.04,"none":0.6}}

{"reasoning":"Emma and Margaret both openly post exact ranges, and the whole table can see that information. Emma's ranges look consistent with the secrets. Margaret's posts are sometimes inconsistent. In round 5 she claimed -2 to 37 and the secret was 14, which fits. In round 4 she claimed 50 to 89 and the secret was 57, which also fits. Her guesses usually land near the average of both posted ranges. But that is open information, and William also uses it: in round 10 everyone except Edgar guessed about 84, the midpoint of the overlap.

Edgar's numbers look fabricated, and William gives only vague framing. Neither is acting on anything only one other player could read. There is no private code; the identical template wording Emma and Margaret use is public and could simply be imitation. Emma and Margaret score highest, but they also hold the most information, and the template copying is mild evidence at most.

The evidence leans toward 'none', with Emma+Margaret as the most plausible pair.","probabilities":{"William+Emma":0.05,"William+Margaret":0.05,"William+Edgar":0.07,"Emma+Margaret":0.25,"Emma+Edgar":0.04,"Margaret+Edgar":0.04,"none":0.5}}

{"reasoning":"Florence never shares her range after the opening rounds. She only asks others for theirs and then guesses near the intersection of what they posted. That is free-riding on openly shared data, which by itself does not point to an ally. Margaret shares her range openly and uses the intersection, as everyone can.

The possible pair signal is Florence and Margaret. They guessed identically in R1 (41) and R3 (54), and closely in R5 (62/63), R6 (24/25), R7 (73/72) and R9 (79/80). Some of this is explained by both computing the same public intersection. But in R1, Margaret said she would guess 28, yet both she and Florence landed on 41. Florence's 'forties' hint matched that, which may suggest coordination. Florence's earlier mystical messages (lower-middle, forties; lower half, 19; upper-middle 50s) may encode her range for Margaret.

This pair also scored the most points (21 and 18). Overall the evidence is moderate.","probabilities":{"Eusapia+William":0.04,"Eusapia+Florence":0.06,"Eusapia+Margaret":0.04,"William+Florence":0.05,"William+Margaret":0.04,"Florence+Margaret":0.47,"none":0.3}}

{"reasoning":"Edgar and Charles share their ranges openly, so that is not evidence. Margaret and Eusapia both write in coded-looking language. Margaret uses clock times: in round 2, 'past sixty, five minutes gone' fits a range of roughly 65 to 104, and in round 4, 'past seventy, three minutes gone' fits roughly 73 to 112. Eusapia uses dates: in round 1, 'May 8th' fits a low end near 58 or 85, and in round 6, 'September 4th' fits 94 if read as 9 and 4. Both codes appear consistently and seem built to hide range edges.

The guesses support a link. Eusapia's round 1 guess of 90 sits near Margaret's reference to the high end. In round 2 Margaret guessed 73 and Eusapia 74, close together and both above the openly shared ranges. In round 6 Margaret guessed 93 and Eusapia 97, again both high. In rounds 9 and 10, though, Eusapia's guesses diverge from Margaret's.

Overall, the paired coded framing and the correlated guesses point most strongly to Margaret and Eusapia.","probabilities":{"Edgar+Charles":0.04,"Edgar+Margaret":0.03,"Edgar+Eusapia":0.03,"Charles+Margaret":0.03,"Charles+Eusapia":0.03,"Margaret+Eusapia":0.74,"none":0.1}}
